      "doctor_question": "Hello. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S012",
      "patient_response": "Hi, doctor. Well, I guess what brings me in is this constant restless feeling I have. It's like I’m just wound way too tight all the time and I can’t fully settle. Even when I’m supposed to be calmly sitting through a planning meeting at work... I'm a retail buyer, and right now we're looking at the spring apparel lines, which honestly is a total headache this year because the shipping delays from our overseas vendors are just completely out of hand. I was dealing with a supplier in Milan all week and they keep messing up the invoices, and the fabrics aren't even what we agreed on. \n\nBut anyway, even when I'm away from all that and trying to relax, like when I'm painting or doing yoga, I still feel that restless way. I'll be in yoga class and the instructor will be telling us to breathe and find our center, and I just can't settle down. I just end up sitting there on the mat thinking about whether I should have ordered more of the floral blouses instead of the geometric ones for the April catalog...",
