    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "About how long have you been feeling this restless and wound up?",
      "targeted_symptom": "duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, it’s been noticeably harder to manage for... I'd say about two years and two months? That’s really when the in-law conflicts started taking over more of our evenings. My husband's mother, she just has this habit of coming over right when we're trying to wind down, and she always brings her little Pomeranian. Which, don't get me wrong, I like dogs, but it sheds everywhere. \n\nI had just bought this beautiful cream-colored rug for the living room—it’s a Moroccan trellis pattern, absolutely gorgeous, I actually got a fantastic deal on it through some wholesale home goods connections at work—and she just lets the dog run all over it with dirty paws. And then she starts making these little passive-aggressive comments about how I'm maintaining the house, and my husband just sits there watching the news! It’s just so frustrating. I mean, I spend my whole day negotiating with international vendors and dealing with shipping manifests, I don't want to come home and negotiate boundaries in my own living room while picking dog hair off a wool rug... \n\nWait, I'm sorry, what did you ask me? Oh, right, the timeline. But yes, about two years and a couple of months since it got really hard to manage.",
