    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Do you find it difficult to control or stop these worries once they start?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Well, it's not so much that I worry, it's more just... I can't stop moving or doing things. Like I said, I'm just wound tight. I don't really sit around and fret about things, I just feel like I need to be up and doing something. Which is why it's so annoying when my mother-in-law comes over, because I'll be right in the middle of trying to organize the pantry or something—I just got these amazing clear acrylic bins, they were on clearance at a home goods show I went to in Chicago last month. The show was actually really disappointing overall, the vendors didn't have anything fresh, just the same old farmhouse chic stuff that's been out for five years. But the bins were a great find. \n\nAnyway, I'll be trying to organize, and she'll come in and just expect me to sit down and have tea and chat, and I just can't. I literally can't just sit there on the sofa while there are things to do. I end up pacing around the kitchen island while she talks. So, no, it's not really worries that I can't stop. It's just the physical feeling of needing to go, go, go.",
