    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Over these past two years, have you also had periods where you felt down, depressed, or had very low energy?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "No, I wouldn't say I feel down or depressed. I definitely don't have low energy, that's for sure! I mean, I'm always on the move. Even when I'm exhausted, my body just wants to keep going. It's like I have this motor inside me that just won't shut off. \n\nSpeaking of motors, my husband just bought this vintage sports car—an old MG from the 70s. He's been spending every weekend in the garage tinkering with it. He says it's his \"midlife crisis\" project, but honestly, it just smells like oil and old leather in there. And he tracked grease onto the driveway, which I had just power-washed. I spent an entire Saturday morning out there with the pressure washer, which, by the way, is incredibly satisfying. Have you ever used one? Watching the dirt just blast away from the concrete... it's amazing. I actually thought about starting a little side business doing power washing because it's so fun, but then I remembered I already have a full-time job dealing with those overseas shipping manifests, which are a nightmare right now. \n\nBut anyway, no, I don't really get depressed or low energy. I just have too much energy, if anything.",
