    {
      "turn": 5,
      "doctor_question": "Looking back to when you were a child before age 12, were you also very restless, constantly on the go, or having trouble sitting still?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Oh, definitely. I remember back in elementary school, my parents were always getting notes sent home from my teachers because I just kept popping out of my seat during lessons. I was always talking over my classmates, too, and I'd just rush to blurt out the answers before the teacher even finished asking the question. I just couldn't wait! \n\nSpeaking of notes, my mother actually kept all of those old school reports in this massive scrapbook. She is absolutely obsessed with scrapbooking. She goes to these huge craft conventions—actually, I went with her to one in Orlando a few years ago because I was scouting some boutique paper vendors for a potential retail line at work. The markup on specialty cardstock is unbelievable, by the way. You wouldn't believe what people will pay for some embossed vellum and a bit of gold foil. We ended up not going with that supplier, though, because their shipping terms were completely ridiculous and inflexible. I mean, if you can't guarantee a net-30 payment structure and reliable freight, I can't work with you. \n\nBut anyway... yes, I was definitely like this back then too. Always jumping out of my chair and talking out of turn.",
